Drop the @CFLAGS@/@CXXFLAGS@ sed stages from the esp32_toolchain.cmake rule.

IDF 5.5 passes compiler flags via a response file, so CFLAGS_INTERNAL expands to
@"/workspace/build/toolchain/cflags". The rule builds its sed expressions with
$(subst /,\/,...), which escapes the slashes but not the @ or the quotes -- sed
then reads the remainder as a filename, exits non-zero, and the pipeline writes
an empty esp32_toolchain.cmake. With no toolchain, CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is never
Generic, so Micro-XRCE-DDS-Client selects its POSIX transport and fails on
sys/socket.h when cross-compiling for xtensa.

esp32_toolchain.cmake.in contains no @CFLAGS@ or @CXXFLAGS@ placeholders, so
these two stages substitute nothing and only ever broke the pipe.

diff --git a/libmicroros.mk b/libmicroros.mk
index e5d22e2..fc0ad8d 100644
--- a/libmicroros.mk
+++ b/libmicroros.mk
@@ -27,8 +27,6 @@ $(EXTENSIONS_DIR)/esp32_toolchain.cmake: $(EXTENSIONS_DIR)/esp32_toolchain.cmake
 	cat $(EXTENSIONS_DIR)/esp32_toolchain.cmake.in | \
 		sed "s/@CMAKE_C_COMPILER@/$(subst /,\/,$(X_CC))/g" | \
 		sed "s/@CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER@/$(subst /,\/,$(X_CXX))/g" | \
-		sed "s/@CFLAGS@/$(subst /,\/,$(CFLAGS_INTERNAL))/g" | \
-		sed "s/@CXXFLAGS@/$(subst /,\/,$(CXXFLAGS_INTERNAL))/g" | \
 		sed "s/@IDF_TARGET@/$(subst /,\/,$(IDF_TARGET))/g" | \
 		sed "s/@IDF_PATH@/$(subst /,\/,$(IDF_PATH))/g" | \
 		sed "s/@BUILD_CONFIG_DIR@/$(subst /,\/,$(BUILD_DIR)/config)/g" \
